  population, NESTED directories (their own rows, never inherited) : 232

THE 2x2 -- AUTHORSHIP on one axis, AUDITABILITY on the other. Both axes over ONE population.
  declared  (162) | code reader opens it :  12   | nothing RUNS opens it : 130   (ORPHAN 102, UNVERIFIABLE 28)
  undeclared     | code reader opens it :   6   | nothing RUNS opens it :  92   (CITED 35, INERT 57)

WHAT EACH QUESTION ALONE MISSES, MEASURED ON THIS SAME POPULATION:
  (a) 'is a declaration PRESENT?' alone PASSES 162 (every declared row) and MISSES 130 of them -- a declaration nothing opens.
  (b) 'is there a READER?' alone PASSES  18 (a CODE reader outside the subtree) and MISSES   6 -- a directory a gate genuinely opens that holds
      no declaration at all. The first version of this line printed 12 for (a): that is the
      (a)AND(b) cell, so the sentence called a passing-row count a question-alone count.
  THE OFF-DIAGONALS ARE 130 AND 6 ROWS OF 269: NEAR-DISJOINT. Neither question half-sees the tree.

THE THIRD SENSE -- IS A READER A WITNESS OR A SYMPTOM? A reader is something that RUNS.
  rows whose ONLY code readers are ENTRY POINTS CARRYING NO TIME BOUND : 28
  `slowgate` measured 105 of 129 gate entry points carry no bound and 1 hangs forever, so a
  reader that cannot be shown to complete is NOT counted as opening anything: it has its own
  cell, and it is NOT counted in either column of the 2x2 above. That is the third sense in
  which 'declared' cannot be the property -- and it is the one nobody has named.

AND THE FOURTH, WHICH IS THE BIGGER ONE -- WHERE THE READER LIVES. A reader inside
  `.agents/slop/` is a PEER: another agent's scratch script, in the tree this file sweeps, on
  the same clock, uncommitted by anyone. It is not a witness. Reader INSTANCES by home:
      4190 (94%)  in-slop peer
       127 ( 2%)  elsewhere
        81 ( 1%)  checks/
        39 ( 0%)  gates/
  MEASURED over 4437 reader instances in this same population. So the 'opened' axis is
  almost entirely PEERS CITING PEERS, and a census that reports '140 directories are opened'
  as AUDITABILITY is reporting that agents mentioned each other.
  top-level directories cited ONLY by in-slop peers and by NOTHING outside : 139
  THE FIRST VERSION OF THIS LINE PRINTED 0 while the rows said 139: it tested the FIRST
  reader PATH (`not r['prose']`, and `'-'` is truthy) instead of the COUNT. A zero that
  disagrees with its own rows file is a `residue.py`, so the line is kept with both.

THE NESTING ROW -- a declaration is about a DIRECTORY, not about its subtree:
  NESTED directories holding a declaration of their OWN : 0 of 232
  NESTED directories that are undeclared while their PARENT is declared : 56
  A walk that INHERITED would green those by inheriting a fact about a different directory.
  This file does not inherit: depth is the directory's own, and every nested directory is a
  row of its own.

